# Run history from the companion scripts. Local to whoever ran them, and it
# carries their timestamps -- no reason for anybody else to have it.
tools/*.log

# Battle.net API credentials, if the Blizzard probe is ever used. A client
# secret is a password: it must never reach a repository, and least of all one
# that becomes a public addon.
tools/blizzard-credentials.txt

# What the passes remember between runs. All of it rebuilds itself, none of it
# means anything on another machine, and together it is about 1.5 MB -- more
# than the addon's own source.
#
#   Baseline-*    where everybody stood last time, for the change columns
#   LiveCache-*   each character's last self-report, for conditional requests
#   SpecsSeen-*   every character ever asked about, so the rolling slice works
#   InspectSeen-* games played when gear was last read, for carry-forward
tools/Baseline-*.txt
tools/LiveCache-*.txt
tools/SpecsSeen-*.txt
tools/InspectSeen-*.txt
tools/SnapshotHistory.txt

# One run's claim on a region. Holds a pid, and a stale one from somebody else's
# machine would be read as a run in progress.
tools/*.lock
tools/*.progress

# Which intervals this machine's dashboard is set to, and where it puts itself.
tools/dashboard-settings.txt

# Built from ArenaPlusDashboard.cs by Build.cmd, using the csc.exe that ships
# with the .NET Framework. The source is here; the binary is a build artefact,
# and a committed .exe in an addon repository is a thing users are right to
# distrust.
tools/ArenaPlusDashboard.exe

# Windows and macOS leave these lying about.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Deliberately NOT ignored, despite being generated:
#
#   Cutoffs.lua
#   Leaderboard.lua
#
# Both are written by tools\UpdateCutoffs.ps1 and tools\UpdateLeaderboard.ps1,
# which looks like a reason to keep them out of the repository. It is the
# opposite. Addons cannot reach the network, so these files *are* the data --
# somebody installing from CurseForge has no scripts, no scheduled task and no
# way to produce them. Ignore them and the addon ships with no cutoffs and an
# empty ladder.
#
# They are committed on purpose, and whatever ends up doing the release should
# make sure the newest scrape is in the build.

# Left over from the talent solver, which was deleted once the client turned
# out to answer GetTalentInfoByID directly. Nothing reads it any more.
tools/TalentGrid.txt
